   "by": "handcheck-research",
   "run": "handcheck-2026-10-23",
   "note": "card contested, the bank narrowed to what is settled (tp-379/3, u10): The card asks when the hammock was invented (100/500/1,000 years ago); the fact asked something else (the Taíno origin of the word), so it was corrected in place. No source dates the invention: hammocks were in use in the Caribbean when Columbus arrived in 1492 (an English canvas hanging bed appears c. 1330); the popular '1,000 years' (Maya) claim is undocumented, and Wikipedia says Maya hammocks came from the Caribbean less than two centuries before the conquest. Answer narrowed to 'more than 500 years ago', with '1,000 years' accepted in the notes."
  },
